## Moral

Grief is not a cage; it is a compass. It points to what we loved, and by extension, what we are capable of loving again. We do not honor the past by living in it, nor do we honor the present by forgetting it. True healing comes when we can carry our history without letting it carry us. Belonging is not about replacing what was lost; it is about making room for what is here. You can be who you were, and who you are, and who you are becoming, all at once. The heart is big enough for all of it.

