## Post-Credit Scene
The next morning, Esmeralda finds Catnip sitting by the pond, watching the water. She sits beside him, her massive form casting a cool shadow.

"You okay, cher?" she asks.

Catnip doesn't look at her. He just nods. "Yeah. Just... thinking."

"About what?"

"About swimming," he lies.

Esmeralda smiles, her dark-honey eyes crinkling. "Well, if you ever want to try, I'll be here. No rush. We got time."

Catnip looks at her, then at the water, then back at her. For a second, he considers it. Then he shakes his head.

"Nah. I'm good here."

But he doesn't move away. He stays, sitting shoulder-to-scale with the croc-a-gator, watching the ripples spread across the pond, content to just be near the water, without having to dive in.

